/target
# The Windows installer's output directory (OutputDir in
# packaging/windows/mindfork.iss). CI builds it on a runner and uploads it;
# locally it appears whenever someone compiles the script by hand, which
# docs/research/inno-setup-7.md invites.
/dist/
__pycache__/
# Website (site/, docs/research/mindfork-io-website.md): build output and the
# brand assets mirrored from assets/ by tools/site_sync_assets.py.
site/public/
site/static/screenshots/
site/static/brand/
site/static/favicon.ico
# Coverage report for SonarQube Cloud (`cargo llvm-cov`, .github/workflows/ci.yml).
/lcov.info
# Editor state. Written by VS Code / Cursor when the SonarQube IDE extension
# binds the workspace; its `connectionId` names a connection local to one
# machine, and the only shareable part -- the project key -- is already in
# `sonar-project.properties`, which is what CI and the tooling read. A binding
# meant to be shared belongs in the portable `.sonarlint/connectedMode.json`
# instead.
/.vscode/
# The containerised test environment (docker/, docs/research/docker-jupyter-env.md):
# the local `.env` copied from `.env.example` (it can hold cloud API keys) and
# whatever gets dropped into the host folder the lab mounts as `~/work`.
/docker/.env
/docker/work/*
!/docker/work/.gitkeep
